    steps:["Melt 4 tbsp of the butter in a small saucepan; stir in the brown sugar and heat until bubbly. Stir in the corn syrup and cream and heat, stirring constantly, just to boiling (don’t cook). Add the nuts (the mixture will be thin). Pour into a buttered 10-inch bundt pan and let stand while continuing.","Sift the flour, baking powder and salt onto waxed paper. Beat the remaining butter until soft in a large bowl. Gradually beat in the sugar. Beat in the egg yolks, chocolate and vanilla until combined.","Add the flour mixture alternately with the milk, beginning and ending with the flour.","Beat the egg whites until stiff and fold into the cake batter. Spoon the batter evenly over the nut mixture in the pan.","Bake at 350° for 45 minutes. Loosen the cake from the edges with a small knife and invert onto a plate. Serve warm with whipped or sour cream."],
